{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/631469-conspiracy-oakley-institute-monster-tamers","id":631469,"title":"Conspiracy: Oakley Institute - Monster Tamers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-18T13:25:48-07:00","id":631469,"title":"Conspiracy: Oakley Institute - Monster Tamers","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[The picture is of a doctor kneeling down towards a boy with a red baseball cap. Behind him are small creatures, mostly animal like, but featuring traits that seem outright strange. He holds a small device, small enough to fit in the child\u2019s palm.]</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Gotta Catch 'Em All!</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Monsters have always lurked among mankind, hiding in the forests, under bridges, within the darkness beneath our beds. Many of these creatures possess are powers and abilities above what humans are capable of, from causing earthquakes to breathing fire and shooting out lightning. Monsters are often savage and territorial, like animals were far more power than they should have.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">...But they\u2019re still just animals. Through out history, humans have tried to control many of these creatures, to bring them under heel. The results are mixed, most monsters are simply too fierce, too powerful. Others proved to be too human and ironically incapable of accepting \u201cdomestication\u201d. Still, people have tried, often hiding their attempts from the world at large, largely in secret.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However, things changed within the past thirty years. A brilliant, yet secretive cabal of environmentalists and researchers managed to figure out a solution, a way to tame the beasts that threatened them. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Named for the head researcher of the project. The Oakley Device was small enough that a child could fit in his palms and possessed many unique and powerful abilities. Its light alone could pacify the simple and animalistic creatures of the world, but taken further, this beam could draw a creature into itself, effectively trapping it in the device. When released, the beast is no longer as feral as it once was and obeyed the whims of its new master. And that was just the start. The machine responded to the wearer\u2019s emotions and desires, allowing the creatures taken into it to act as conduits for their master\u2019s will.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suddenly, the beasts in the fields that could terrorize villages by themselves seemed no longer as frightening, for humankind had its own beasts to combat it. Creatures of flame found themselves fighting creatures of water, living shadows faced the light. More monsters could be captured and brought for the human cause. It seemed as though humankind was now in greater position to sieze even more control over the world, mass production of the so called Oakley Devices.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yet that didn\u2019t happen. The day before the grand unveiling, heavenly and hellish beings descended and destroyed the research lab and slew many of those responsible for the device. Thousands of hand held miracle machines were disposed of in one fell swoop. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now, none know how the devices came to be, the technology that made them was lost. All that remains now are a small handful of what was meant to be start of a whole new world. Rebranding themselves as the Oakley Institute, in honor of the long gone inventor, the semisecret society stirs.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Today, they run a recruitment drive, bringing in young folks and showing them the supernatural world, but in a different light towards it than other conspiracies. To them, it doesn\u2019t matter if a lizard breathes fire; it might be a young dragon, but that means it must still be cared for like any pet, albeit with more care. And sometimes, the kids take them home, hiding them within the small pocket universe that anyone can hold\u2026 and the adults in particular often carry small armies wherever they go. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The operation is small, and mostly secretive for now; they don\u2019t want a repeat of last time, but who knows what\u2019ll happen in the future?</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Storytelling:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You\u2019ve been doing this since you were in grade school. You and your friends were once trapped in another dimension when all you really wanted to do at stay at Summer Camp. In retrospect, it was a blast, you met your partner then. Although no one will ever forget the fact that you used to wear goggles everywhere you went.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You and your sisters were all accepted at the institute, but you know you\u2019re the only one with any talent, no matter how much they said they had the looks. That was fine by you, you could kick their asses. Besides, you needed them to help gather money for that aquarium\u2026 or gymnasium. You\u2019re still not sure which yet. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">After your brother died, you went through his things. You found what you thought to be a toy of his, you didn\u2019t understand what you had possessed real power, not until you abused it and caused far more suffering than you know what to do with. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Status: </span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">0 - </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You\u2019re not all that experienced controlling the creatures yet, but you\u2019re a Tamer now. You still fear them, but at least now you got the power. You may be just a kid or a young man, all told, but you signed up and that\u2019s what counts. You possess an Oakley Device and a Partner and may spend merits to modify them.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">000 - </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You\u2019re not as young as you used to be, that much is clear. You\u2019ve traveled far and met many of the strange and wondrous creatures that inhabit our world, maybe spent years on it. You know them well. You may choose to reroll any failure or dramatic failure that results from any social rolls dealing with nonsapient creatures.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">00000 </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>-</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the ten year olds dream about being the best Tamer, they were talking about being like you. Sure, you don\u2019t travel as much as you used to when you were young, but your adventures are the stuff of legend. At this point, you control creatures that in some other time might have been thought of as minor gods. You gain the Inspiring merit for free.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Endowment: Oakley Device </span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While most of the Oakley Devices have been destroyed during the purge, many still remain to be used.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The device may capture and hold supernatural creatures inside of it, sealing them inside its internal pocket dimension.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Capturing a monster requires (think of rules later)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once captured, any of number creatures may be let out of the pocket dimension in a nonhostile state. Such creatures possess their usual natural behaviors with the sole except that they are not actively aggressive towards humans and will flee when attacked.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However, creatures let out of the Oakley Device may be used in combat. Doing so is taxing and requires that the user must spend a willpower point to conjure his creature in a combat ready form. Only one such creature may be out when released in this manner. Summoning another creature causes the other to be recalled into the device. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Controlling a combat creature is mentally taxing and as a result the creature has no instant actions of its own. In order for it to possess instant actions, you must forgo your own, in effect, spending your own action to give orders.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With the exception of Partner creatures (see below), any creature slain when released from the Oakley device are slain and are effectively dead.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Partner Creature </span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some creatures possess a stronger link to the Oakley device than others. Said creatures are often somewhat exceptional examples of their kind, some even possessing a rudimentary understanding of language before capture and often submissive. Said creatures do not die easily and when they fall in combat are simply forced to return to their owner\u2019s device.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By default, all newly christened and fully fledged Tamers receive a Partner creature as such creatures are often breeded in large enough numbers to be seen as successful examples of domestication, for a small and scattered group that is.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(To define, stats)</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shared Will: (00)</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As the Oakley Devices act as a bridge between man and magical creatures, it stands to reason then that the human will can sometimes crossover it. The Tamer may spend Willpower to pay willpower costs for his creature. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Capacity: (--- or 0 to 00000): </span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oakley Devices might contain small pocket dimensions, but there is a hard limit to the number of different creatures that they could store. By default, Oakley Devices may store a single creature, typically a Tamer\u2019s first partner. Though, the Tamer may force and exert his will over the device, forcing it to increase how much it can contain. Each dot in this merit raises the maximum creature capacity of the Tamer\u2019s Oakley device by 1 up to a maximum of 6 at 5 dots.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yes, I am very aware I just made a Pokemon/Digimon themed Conspiracy. You can probably tell based on the numerous and unsubtle references in the post. I figured why not!<br /> <br /> I just wish I had better foresight and naming ideas and that I could think up better mechanics and fill in the gaps. Oh well, perhaps you folks have ideas... provided you guys aren't too busy laughing at how silly this is.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 08-18-2015, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T13:35:49-07:00","id":631495,"title":"","content":"gotta catch them all! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T15:31:30-07:00","id":631655,"title":"","content":"Well, hey, no one's did monster pets in NWoD as a hunter endowment, so why not?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now all I gotta figure out is how I want to make the system for having companions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T20:09:31-07:00","id":631840,"title":"","content":"I love this, I'm using this, I'll probably toss ideas at you along the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T20:29:31-07:00","id":631850,"title":"","content":"Well, I am glad you like it then.<br /> <br /> The questions on my lips are right now, what're you going to use it for since this project appealed to you enough to be &quot;game worthy&quot;?<br /> <br /> And what ideas can you give me about... stating up or deciding how the game should handle &quot;supernatural creatures&quot;? As in, stats wise. I'm kinda fuzzy about that. Thought of doing statistics blocks, but I'm apprehensive about it. Same with &quot;build it yourself&quot; style powers. Maybe use Dread Powers and Numina for monster powers?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T22:32:02-07:00","id":631914,"title":"","content":"Hmm, maybe it's just me, but I really want to go pokethulu with them and have them be tamers of things adults weren't meant to know- they're enemies being cthonic cults that don't appreciate their deities being put in red and white balls. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T06:34:17-07:00","id":632200,"title":"","content":"What kind of &quot;monsters&quot; can be tamed? Can a tamer get Solomon Birch in his pok...device?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T07:48:13-07:00","id":632285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/631469-conspiracy-oakley-institute-monster-tamers?p=632200#post632200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of &quot;monsters&quot; can be tamed? Can a tamer get Solomon Birch in his pok...device?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I believe I stated that animal like supernaturals are valid. Anything that can be described as human level in terms of intelligence can't be snagged, so no people.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... Hellhounds, possible. Demons, beastial and unintelligent ones, yeah. Living shadows and rocks, yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> The idea of the Conspiracy is that they're a group of animal trainers and environmentalists... with super pets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T15:49:41-07:00","id":633896,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The creatures under the Oakley Institute\u2019s control are a wide bunch, ranging from living shadows and rocks, to slightly more mundane things like flaming roosters and seals that breathe frost. This is made more complicated when some monsters somehow\u2026 evolve into stranger, more advanced forms. Some creatures, despite their animalistic behavior are able to possess inhuman cunning and problem solving when it comes to certain fields.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As a general rule and as a system for classification, Oakley agents figured out that it was best to separate monsters into different levels, defining the rough capability and power of a specific creature. Some creatures, particularly those well trained achieve statistics above the norm.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In game terms: creatures have their statistics determined by Level, in a similar manner to Rank for spirits. Level determines attribute caps, with a seperate limit for mental and social attributes. As level goes up, the so do the number of dots. Level also is substituted for Power Stat when a Power Stat like trait is required to be resisted upon.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Creatures, before factoring Level (Level 0), possess 1 dot in each attribute, no skills, a default size of 2, and no dread powers. The chart below lists how powerful a monster grows at certain levels.</span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 800px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Level</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Physical Cap</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Mental/Social Cap</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Attribute Dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Skill Dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Boost</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Dread Power dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Willpower cost</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">0</td> <td cl