 <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">25</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each point of Boost may be spent on increasing monster size by 1 or increasing the monster\u2019s storage of willpower by 1.<br /> <br /> <br /> Because of how variable monsters are, it is best advised Storytellers use their better judgement when allowing Tamers access to multiple monsters.<br /> Additionally, high Level monsters require proportionately more energy to coerce and conjure using the Oakley device as defined by &quot;Willpower cost&quot;, representing the psychic effort the user must expend to summon and control the beast in a combat setting. In a noncombat, nonhazardous environment, the Willpower cost does not need to be paid as the creature is naturally willing to want to level the Oakley Device when able; creatures simply don't want to fight most of the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Alright, experimental idea I've been tossing around and it makes high tier monsters... high tier. I'm not even going to assign dots to these.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit